@startuml domain-model
' Sources: docs/design/requirements.md, sections "Domain Entities", "Values",
' "Relationships and Multiplicities", "Inheritance", "Interfaces", and
' "Composition over Inheritance", for the classes and relationships.
' tools/models/ (Phase 06) for the attributes, methods, object references, collections,
' inheritance, and abstract classes.
' Attributes are private (-) and exposed as read-only @property (+). No setters.
' Subclasses list only the members they define or override; inherited members are not repeated.
' {abstract} marks an @abstractmethod. Abstract classes inherit from ABC.
' Collections are private typed lists; their getters return tuples.
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members

' ---------- Currency pair, trade setups, and backtests ----------

class CurrencyPair {
  - _name : str
  - _price_data : tuple[tuple[float, float], ...]
  - _backtests : list[BacktestResult]
  + __init__(name : str, price_data)
  .. read-only properties ..
  + name : str
  + price_data : tuple[tuple[float, float], ...]
  + backtests : tuple[BacktestResult, ...]
  .. methods ..
  + market_structure() : str
  + pip_size() : float
  + pip_value_per_lot(price : float) : float
  - _holds(result : BacktestResult) : bool
  + add_backtest(result : BacktestResult)
  + remove_backtest(result : BacktestResult)
  + latest_backtest() : BacktestResult | None
}

class TradeSetup {
  - _pair : CurrencyPair
  - _direction : TradeDirection
  - _entry : float
  - _stop_loss : float
  - _take_profit : float
  + __init__(pair : CurrencyPair, direction : TradeDirection, entry : float, stop_loss : float, take_profit : float)
  .. read-only properties ..
  + pair : CurrencyPair
  + pair_name : str
  + trade_direction : TradeDirection
  + direction : str
  + entry : float
  + stop_loss : float
  + take_profit : float
  .. methods ..
  + reward() : float
  + risk() : float
  + reward_to_risk() : float
  + outcome() : str
}

note right of TradeSetup
  Concrete class (Phase 06). Delegates the price-order check,
  reward, risk, and outcome to its TradeDirection.
  Used through its type by the module-level function
  in trade_setup.py:
  + evaluate_setup(setup : TradeSetup) : str
end note

abstract class TradeDirection {
  .. read-only properties ..
  + {abstract} name : str
  + {abstract} units_sign : int
  .. methods ..
  + {abstract} check_price_order(entry : float, stop_loss : float, take_profit : float)
  + {abstract} reward(entry : float, take_profit : float) : float
  + {abstract} risk(entry : float, stop_loss : float) : float
  + {abstract} outcome(price_data, stop_loss : float, take_profit : float) : str
  + {abstract} is_beyond(price : float, reference : float) : bool
}

note right of TradeDirection
  Interface (ABC): a bare TradeDirection
  cannot be created (TypeError).
  Holds no state.
end note

class BuyDirection {
  .. read-only properties ..
  + name : str
  + units_sign : int
  .. methods ..
  + check_price_order(entry : float, stop_loss : float, take_profit : float)
  + reward(entry : float, take_profit : float) : float
  + risk(entry : float, stop_loss : float) : float
  + outcome(price_data, stop_loss : float, take_profit : float) : str
  + is_beyond(price : float, reference : float) : bool
}

class SellDirection {
  .. read-only properties ..
  + name : str
  + units_sign : int
  .. methods ..
  + check_price_order(entry : float, stop_loss : float, take_profit : float)
  + reward(entry : float, take_profit : float) : float
  + risk(entry : float, stop_loss : float) : float
  + outcome(price_data, stop_loss : float, take_profit : float) : str
  + is_beyond(price : float, reference : float) : bool
}

TradeDirection <|-- BuyDirection
TradeDirection <|-- SellDirection

class BacktestResult {
  - _pair : CurrencyPair
  - _test_date : date
  - _setups : list[TradeSetup]
  + __init__(pair : CurrencyPair, test_date : date)
  .. read-only properties ..
  + pair : CurrencyPair
  + pair_name : str
  + test_date : date
  + setups : tuple[TradeSetup, ...]
  + setups_tested : int
  + trade_count : int
  + win_count : int
  .. methods ..
  - _holds(setup : TradeSetup) : bool
  + add_setup(setup : TradeSetup)
  + remove_setup(setup : TradeSetup)
  + win_rate() : float | None
}

CurrencyPair "1" <-- "0..*" TradeSetup : has >
CurrencyPair "1" -- "0..*" BacktestResult : has >
BacktestResult "0..1" o--> "0..*" TradeSetup : is based on >
TradeSetup "0..*" --> "1" TradeDirection : follows the rules of >

note "All trade setups in a backtest result must belong\nto the same currency pair (same object) as that backtest result.\nA trade setup belongs to at most one backtest result:\ndocumented only, not enforced." as SamePair
